  "articleBody": "A leaking shower after a renovation is a real headache and often points to issues with the bathroom waterproofing. Many folks mistakenly think that tile and grout alone are enough to prevent water from reaching the structure, but that's just not the case. If the waterproofing system wasn't installed correctly, or if it was skipped entirely, water can easily seep through. Common mistakes include inconsistent application of the waterproofing membrane, not properly sealing corners or joints, or using incompatible products that don't form a continuous barrier. Hidden moisture damage from before the renovation, or structural movement that wasn't addressed, can also compromise even a well-intentioned waterproofing effort. It's crucial that any waterproofing materials, adhesives, and sealants fully cure according to manufacturer instructions before the area sees any water. If you're dealing with a leak, it's definitely time to get a professional involved to prevent further, potentially costly, hidden damage.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}